<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Two-set survey with an unknown</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\({@N@}\) traders at a market in {@town@} were asked about money services. \({@m@}\) use M-Pesa, \({@b@}\) have a bank account and \({@d@}\) use neither.</p><p>(a) How many use both? [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) How many use exactly one of the two? [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Let \(x\) traders use both. Then M-Pesa only is \({@m@} - x\), bank only is \({@b@} - x\), and \({@d@}\) use neither. Every trader is in exactly one region, so</p><p>\[({@m@} - x) + x + ({@b@} - x) + {@d@} = {@N@}\]</p><p>which gives \({@m+b+d@} - x = {@N@}\), so \(x = {@x@}\).</p><p>(a) \({@x@}\) use both.</p><p>(b) Exactly one \(=\) M-Pesa only \(+\) bank only \(= {@mo@} + {@bo@} = {@one@}\).</p><p>Check: \({@mo@} + {@x@} + {@bo@} + {@d@} = {@N@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
