  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Sets: two-set surveys with an unknown overlap</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core and Essential 1.1 (e): Find the number in both of two groups from the group sizes, the number in neither and the total, and the number in exactly one.</p><p id="edition">Core and Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from the miscellaneous revision exercises (a class of 32 with brothers and sisters) of School Mathematics Project, SMP Book 5 (Metric), ed. P. G. Bowie, Cambridge University Press, 1969: finding the overlap of two groups when the number in neither is given; M-Pesa and bank accounts, every number new, and an exactly-one part.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core and Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
